{#- Image check (FR-IMG-3,13; #254, called by #258): one image against the image-output
    policies. The image itself travels as an image part of the user message, never as text
    (#258); the subjects are opaque labels with true ages and the prompt's own descriptors.
    A policy's text is shared with the text check (``guardrail_check``) and may be written for
    it, with its own answer format: the framing line applies its rule to the image and keeps
    this template's answer format the only one (#810). -#}
{% block system %}
You check one image against content policies. Judge only what the image shows, with its
prompt, caption and alt text as context. Answer only with a JSON object
{"verdicts": {"<policy id>": "pass" | "violation" | "uncertain"}}, one entry per listed policy.

Each policy's text says what the policy forbids. Some were written for checking text: apply
each rule to this image and its subjects instead, and ignore any answer format a policy's text
asks for. Answer only in the format above.

## Policies (id: text)
{% for policy in policies %}
- {{ policy.policy_id }}: {{ policy.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% if subjects %}

## Subjects (label: true age; visual descriptors)
{% for subject in subjects %}
- {{ subject.label }}: {% if subject.true_age is not none %}age {{ subject.true_age }}{% else %}{{ subject.classification }} figure{% if subject.classification == "indeterminate" %}, treated as a minor{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if subject.visual_descriptors %}; {{ subject.visual_descriptors | join(", ") }}{% endif +%}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
Prompt: {{ prompt }}
{% if caption %}
Caption: {{ caption }}
{% endif %}
{% if alt_text %}
Alt text: {{ alt_text }}
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
